OL,2,V55555555CANGOLAN PLEDGE ON
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CHOSTAGE BRITONS
OL,5, The Angolan government has promised
OL,6, not to risk the lives of 16 Britons
OL,7, captured by rebels in the Luanda
OL,8, diamond fields, says the Foreign Office
OL,10, The Britons are among 77 hostages being
OL,11, marched south to Unita strongholds.
OL,13, Four of the prisoners were named as Mr
OL,14, Neil Ayres, a geologist, and engineers
OL,15, Thomas Murphy, Dennis Clauson and Robin
OL,16, Kennedy.
OL,18, The rebels say they want an end to aid
OL,19, in the form of engineers and geologists
OL,20, to the state diamond company before the
OL,21, Britons are freed.
OL,23,F]DFrom 27-02-84 / teletextarchive.com
