OL,2,V55555555CMIND YOUR LANGUAGE,
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CJEERING MPs TOLD
OL,5, MPs have been given a rap over the
OL,6, knuckles for rowdy behaviour in
OL,7, Parliament during Question Time.
OL,9, Speaker Bernard Weatherill reminded
OL,10, them they had a supreme duty to set
OL,11, an example to the country by ensuring
OL,12, freedom of speech in the Commons.
OL,14, His wigging came after complaints by
OL,15, Labour MP Norman Atkinson about
OL,16, rowdiness and catcalls in a session
OL,17, last week.
OL,19, He described it as the worst he could
OL,20, recall for 20 years.
OL,22,F]D This ORACLE page is from 27-02-84
