OL,2,V55555555C26 SOLDIERS HURT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CIN BUS CRASH
OL,5, Twenty-six British soldiers were
OL,6, injured, four of them seriously, when
OL,7, a bus taking them to a beach holiday
OL,8, in Kenya tumbled into a ravine.
OL,10, The bus had swerved to avoid a
OL,11, pedestrian while travelling from
OL,12, Nairobi to Mombassa, on the Indian
OL,13, Ocean.
OL,15, Eleven of the soldiers, from the Royal
OL,16, Irish Rangers, were admitted to
OL,17, hospital with broken limbs and bruises.
OL,19, The Rangers had just completed a five-
OL,20, week training and survival course in
OL,21, the Nanyuki region of northern Kenya.
OL,23,F]DFrom 27-02-84 / teletextarchive.com
