OL,2,V55555555CONE-HOUR LONDON TRANSPORT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSTRIKE CALLED
OL,5, Union leaders representing London's
OL,6, bus and Tube workers have called for
OL,7, a one-hour stoppage tomorrow over the
OL,8, Government's union ban at GCHQ.
OL,10, The walk-out, between 1pm and 2pm,could
OL,11, mean disruption for up to three hours,
OL,12, but the evening rush should not be hit.
OL,14, Other train and ferry services could
OL,15, also be affected.
OL,17, NUR general secretary Jimmy Knapp has
OL,18, urged members to give "absolute
OL,19, support" wherever possible.
OL,21, But the two main teaching unions - the
OL,22, NUT and NAS/UWT - have decided not to
OL,23, advise their members to strike.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
