OL,2,V55555555CHOWE DEFENDS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CUNION BAN AT GCHQ
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Sir Geoffrey Howe has
OL,6, denied claims that the Government's
OL,7, union ban at GCHQ is the first step to
OL,8, a wider action in the Civil Service.
OL,10, He told a Commons debate two-thirds of
OL,11, the staff there had accepted the
OL,12, Government's #1,000 compensation.
OL,14, Sir Geoffrey maintained that the
OL,15, Government's aim was to ensure
OL,16, continuous operation at Cheltenham.
OL,18, Labour's Denis Healey said the union
OL,19, ban had done "immense damage to morale"
OL,20, in all Government services.
OL,22, The whole machinery of Government was
OL,23, seething with discontent, he said.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
